## Mandatory: Use ops.sh for Remote Operations

<!-- CUSTOMIZE: Remove this section if not using ops.sh -->

**All interaction with the remote server MUST go through `./ops.sh`.** This script provides safety controls.

```bash
./ops.sh help                    # Show all available commands
./ops.sh deploy                  # Deploy to remote server
./ops.sh logs backend            # View backend logs
./ops.sh status                  # Show container status
./ops.sh health                  # Health check all services
./ops.sh db backup               # Create database backup
```

### Safety Tiers

| Tier | Operations | Behavior |
|------|------------|----------|
| **SAFE** | logs, status, health, backup | Execute immediately |
| **MODERATE** | deploy, restart, migrate | Requires confirmation |
| **HUMAN_REQUIRED** | rollback, restore, stop | Human must approve |
| **BLOCKED** | DROP, TRUNCATE, DELETE (raw) | Refused with error |

### Never Do These

| DO NOT | WHY |
|--------|-----|
| Run `ssh` commands directly | Bypasses safety controls |
| Run `docker exec` directly | Can execute destructive operations |
| Run SQL directly on database | No validation, no audit trail |

**If you need to interact with the remote server, use `./ops.sh`. No exceptions.**

